    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.bufremove\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nInvoke command line buffer with q:\r\nInvoke mini.bufremove ( in my case this \\<leader\\>bd )\r\n\r\nAfter I invoke mini.bufremove for the first time I get a Message with E11. After invoking it the second time I get the following message\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua: ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:146: Error executing lua: ...al/share/nvim/la\r\nzy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:155: nvim_exec(): Vim(bprevious):E11: Ungültig im Kommandozeilenfenster; <CR> führt aus, CTR\r\nL-C beendet: bprevious                                                                                                               \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                     \r\n        [C]: in function 'cmd'                                                                                                       \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:155: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/b\r\nufremove.lua:146>                                                                                                                    \r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'                                                                                             \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:146: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/b\r\nufremove.lua:136>                                                                                                                    \r\n        vim/shared.lua: in function 'tbl_map'                                                                                        \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:125: in function 'unshow'                                        \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:213: in function 'delete'                                        \r\n        ...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugins/editor.lua:323: in function <...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugin\r\ns/editor.lua:323>                                                                                                                    \r\nstack traceback:                                                                                                                     \r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'                                                                                             \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:146: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/b\r\nufremove.lua:136>                                                                                                                    \r\n        vim/shared.lua: in function 'tbl_map'                                                                                        \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:125: in function 'unshow'                                        \r\n        ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:213: in function 'delete'                                        \r\n        ...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugins/editor.lua:323: in function <...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugin\r\ns/editor.lua:323>                                \r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be nice, if mini.bufremove would just close this buffer as a :close command does. This special buffer can be identified by its name, which ends with \"[Command Line]\".\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.0-dev-988+gf905ab045-dirty\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nq:\r\n\\<leader\\>bd\r\n\\<leader\\>bd\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nclose Command Line buffer\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nError",
