            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can reproduce this.\r\n\r\n> It would be nice, if mini.bufremove would just close this buffer as a :close command does.\r\n\r\nIt doesn't seem to be the most appropriate course of action, as main purpose of 'mini.bufremove' is to delete buffers without changing window layout. So it *should* work by only removing buffer in that window.\r\n\r\nI'll look into it.",
